{
  "description": "The traffic report (FR-50, FR-51, T-110): what a gate sends to the report address its local policy names. `build`: from the request log entries (as in gate-log), the last cursor `sentUntil` (start of the first hour not yet sent; null = never) and the clock `now`, the gate sends the complete UTC hours since the cursor (at most 24 back, a cursor in the future counts as none), sums per (hour, route): `requests`, status classes `s2`..`s5`, the gate's `errors` by code (the 20 most frequent), `msTotal`, `msMax`; buckets sorted by hour, then route, null last. No client hash, no single request. `expect.report` null = nothing to send yet; `expect.until` = the next cursor once the Cloud took it. `parse`: how Moat Cloud reads a received report at `now` (strict JSON, exact keys, sums consistent, hours on the hour, not in the future and at most 30 days old, each (hour, route) once): `{ok: true, report}` or `{ok: false, code}`.",
  "now": 1798682400,
